            <ArticleTitle>Dramatic headache relief after sumatriptan in a patient with a pituitary macroadenoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>443-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We are reporting an interesting case of pituitary macroadenoma. The patient presented with sudden, bifrontal, pulsating headache; photophobia; and an abducens nerve palsy, due to extension of the tumor into the cavernous sinus region. The headache resolved completely after a subcutaneous injection of sumatriptan.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
